# Programmatically generated De Almeida Qs

section4_en = [{'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'In which year did the Battle of Chaul take place between the Portuguese and a combined Muslim fleet?', 'opts': ['1508 CE', '1505 CE', '1509 CE', '1515 CE'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The Battle of Chaul was fought in March 1508 CE.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Who was the young Portuguese commander who was killed during the Battle of Chaul?', 'opts': ['Lourenço de Almeida', 'Francisco de Almeida', 'Afonso de Albuquerque', 'Duarte Pacheco Pereira'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': "Lourenço de Almeida, the Viceroy's only son, died when his flagship was trapped and sunk."}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Which Egyptian dynasty dispatched the fleet under Amir Husain Al-Kurdi to fight the Portuguese at Chaul?', 'opts': ['The Mamluk Sultanate', 'The Ottoman Empire', 'The Fatimid Caliphate', 'The Ayyubid Dynasty'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The Mamluk Sultanate of Egypt sent the fleet to defend their spice trade interests.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Who was the governor of Diu who commanded the Gujarati fleet and allied with the Mamluks at Chaul?', 'opts': ['Malik Ayyaz', 'Bahadur Shah', 'Muzaffar Shah II', 'Mahmud Begarha'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Malik Ayyaz (a Russian convert and governor of Diu) co-commanded the coalition fleet.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'How did the Battle of Chaul end for the Portuguese fleet?', 'opts': ['It resulted in a decisive defeat and the loss of their flagship', 'It was a decisive Portuguese victory', 'It was a peaceful draw', 'The Portuguese fleet was entirely captured'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The battle was a major defeat for the Portuguese, resulting in the death of Lourenço and loss of his ship.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'Which fleets composed the allied coalition that defeated the Portuguese at Chaul? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['The Mamluk fleet under Amir Husain', 'The Gujarat Sultanate fleet under Malik Ayyaz', "The Zamorin's forces of Calicut", 'The British Royal Navy'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'The coalition consisted of Mamluks, Gujaratis, and Calicut vessels. The British were not involved.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': "Identify the key details of Lourenço de Almeida's death at Chaul. (Select all that apply)", 'opts': ['His flagship was pinned down by a Gujarati cable in the river', 'He refused to retreat or surrender despite being wounded', 'He was struck and killed by a cannonball', 'He was captured and executed in Cairo'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'His ship was trapped by a cable, he refused to surrender, and he was killed by cannon fire. He was not taken to Cairo.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'Which factors contributed to the Portuguese defeat at Chaul? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['The surprise arrival of the Mamluk fleet in Indian waters', 'Tactical entrapment of Portuguese ships in the shallow river harbor', "Malik Ayyaz's coordinate strike with coastal gunboats", 'The mutiny of Portuguese captains during the battle'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': "Surprise arrival of Mamluks, shallow river traps, and Ayyaz's gunboats were key factors. There was no mutiny."}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'What were the immediate political reactions to the Battle of Chaul? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['Francisco de Almeida swore a personal oath of revenge', 'Portuguese prestige in the Indian Ocean was temporarily shattered', 'Almeida refused to transfer power to Albuquerque', 'The Zamorin captured Cochin immediately'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'Almeida swore revenge, Portuguese prestige suffered, and Almeida delayed the power transition. Cochin was not captured.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': "Which details describe Malik Ayyaz's role at the Battle of Chaul? (Select all that apply)", 'opts': ['He served as the governor of Diu', 'He commanded the fast coastal dhows and gunboats of Gujarat', 'He acted cautiously, avoiding complete destruction of the Portuguese fleet to maintain diplomatic leverage', 'He was a Portuguese agent who betrayed the Zamorin'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'Ayyaz was the governor of Diu, commanded the Gujarat fleet, and acted cautiously for diplomatic reasons. He was not a Portuguese agent.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The Battle of Chaul was the first major defeat suffered by the Portuguese in Indian waters.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'It shattered their myth of naval invincibility.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Amir Husain Al-Kurdi was the commander of the Mamluk fleet dispatched from Egypt.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'He led the Mamluk expedition to expel the Portuguese.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Lourenço de Almeida surrendered his ship to Malik Ayyaz before dying.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He refused to surrender and fought until he was killed by a cannonball.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The Battle of Chaul was fought in the open ocean far away from the coast.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'It was fought inside the shallow harbor and estuary of Chaul.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The Portuguese fleet at Chaul was caught by surprise because they did not expect Mamluk intervention.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'They did not know that a Mamluk fleet had arrived in India.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Francisco de Almeida was present and personally commanded the fleet at Chaul.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'The fleet was commanded by his son Lourenço; Francisco was in Cochin.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Malik Ayyaz treated the Portuguese prisoners captured at Chaul with cruelty.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He treated them with relative kindness to preserve diplomatic options with Lisbon.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The battle ended the Mamluk spice monopoly permanently.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'It was a victory for the Mamluks, temporarily securing their trade route.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Battle of Chaul was fought in the month of __________ in 1508.', 'ans': 'March', 'sol': 'The naval clash occurred in March 1508 CE.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Egyptian commander of the fleet at Chaul was Amir __________.', 'ans': 'Husain', 'sol': 'Amir Husain Al-Kurdi led the Mamluk forces.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The governor of Diu who co-commanded the coalition forces was Malik __________.', 'ans': 'Ayyaz', 'sol': 'Malik Ayyaz was the governor of Diu under the Gujarat Sultanate.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': "The Viceroy's son, __________ de Almeida, died in the battle.", 'ans': 'Lourenço', 'sol': 'Lourenço de Almeida was the commander at Chaul.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The flagship at Chaul was trapped when its hull was pierced and it was caught by a sea __________.', 'ans': 'cable', 'sol': 'A cable caught the ship, preventing it from escaping the harbor.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Muslim coalition was backed by the Sultan of Gujarat, Mahmud __________.', 'ans': 'Begarha', 'sol': 'Mahmud Begarha was the famous sultan of Gujarat.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The battle took place in the harbor of __________, a port near modern Mumbai.', 'ans': 'Chaul', 'sol': 'Chaul was a major trade port on the western coast.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Mamluk fleet had been built in the Red Sea using timber supplied by __________.', 'ans': 'Venice', 'sol': 'Venice secretly supplied ship-building timber to help Egypt fight Portugal.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the battle commanders of Chaul with their affiliations:', 'items': [{'left': 'Lourenço de Almeida'}, {'left': 'Amir Husain Al-Kurdi'}, {'left': 'Malik Ayyaz'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'Portuguese Crown fleet'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'Mamluk Sultanate of Egypt'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Gujarat Sultanate (Diu)'}], 'sol': 'Lourenço was Portuguese, Amir Husain Mamluk, and Ayyaz was from Gujarat.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the strategic outcomes of the battle with the corresponding entities:', 'items': [{'left': 'Death of Lourenço'}, {'left': 'Kind treatment of prisoners'}, {'left': 'Supply of shipbuilding timber'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': "Francisco de Almeida's grief and delay of power transfer"}, {'val': '1', 'text': "Malik Ayyaz's cautious diplomacy"}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Venetian covert support to Mamluks'}], 'sol': "Lourenço's death caused Francisco's grief, Ayyaz treated prisoners well, and Venice supplied timber."}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the geographical features of the battle with their significance:', 'items': [{'left': 'Chaul estuary'}, {'left': 'Suez shipyard'}, {'left': 'Diu harbor'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'Shallow water trap for Portuguese naus'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'Construction site of the Mamluk fleet'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Base of the Gujarat coalition fleet'}], 'sol': "Chaul was the shallow trap, Suez was where Mamluks built the fleet, and Diu was Malik Ayyaz's base."}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What weapon killed Lourenço de Almeida?', 'sol': 'Answer: A cannonball. Explanation: He was struck by a cannonball after his legs were shattered by a previous shot.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which European power secretly assisted the Mamluks in building their fleet?', 'sol': 'Answer: Venice. Explanation: Venice wanted to protect its Levantine trade monopoly.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What did Malik Ayyaz do with the surviving Portuguese prisoners?', 'sol': 'Answer: He imprisoned them in Diu and treated them well. Explanation: He kept them as diplomatic hostages.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "How did Lourenço's ship become trapped at Chaul?", 'sol': 'Answer: Its rudder was damaged and it was caught by a fish trap/cable. Explanation: The ship could not maneuver in the shallow estuary.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "Did the Portuguese fleet retreat after Lourenço's death?", 'sol': 'Answer: Yes, the remaining ships withdrew to Cochin. Explanation: The survivors sailed south under the second-in-command.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Who was the sultan of Egypt who ordered the creation of the anti-Portuguese fleet?', 'sol': 'Answer: Al-Ashraf Qansuh al-Ghawri. Explanation: He was the penultimate Mamluk Sultan.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What was the reaction of the Zamorin of Calicut to the Battle of Chaul?', 'sol': 'Answer: He celebrated and sent reinforcements to the Mamluks. Explanation: He hoped to finally expel the Portuguese from Malabar.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Why did the Portuguese not expect the Mamluk fleet at Chaul?', 'sol': 'Answer: They believed the Mamluks lacked the naval capacity to sail into the Indian Ocean. Explanation: The Mamluks had traditionally relied on land armies and lacked a navy.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: The Mamluk fleet was able to surprise the Portuguese at Chaul.\nReason: The Portuguese did not have an active intelligence network in the Red Sea in 1507.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Lack of intelligence allowed the Mamluk fleet to sail to India undetected.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Lourenço de Almeida refused to abandon his flagship.\nReason: He believed that a Portuguese noble commander should never surrender to Muslim forces.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Chivalric codes of honor prevented him from retreating.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Venice secretly supplied timber to the Mamluks to build their war fleet.\nReason: Venice wanted to destroy the Mamluk Sultanate and take over Egypt.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Assertion is true, but Reason is false because Venice wanted to help Egypt preserve the spice route from Portuguese disruption.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Malik Ayyaz was a native Gujarati noble.\nReason: He was born in Ahmedabad and belonged to the royal family of the Gujarat Sultanate.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. Malik Ayyaz was a Russian slave convert who rose to become the governor of Diu.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "Assertion: The Battle of Chaul resulted in the complete destruction of the Portuguese navy in India.\nReason: All 21 ships of Almeida's fleet were sunk during the battle.", 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. Only a few Portuguese ships were lost, including the flagship; the rest withdrew safely.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Francisco de Almeida was devastated by the news of the Battle of Chaul.\nReason: His only son Lourenço was killed, and the Portuguese navy had suffered its first defeat.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The loss of his son transformed his governorship into a campaign of revenge.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Malik Ayyaz treated the Portuguese prisoners kindly.\nReason: He wanted to keep a diplomatic door open with the Viceroy in case the Portuguese retaliated.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Ayyaz acted pragmatically, anticipating a strong Portuguese counter-attack.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: The Battle of Chaul temporarily secured Mamluk-Gujarati control over the Arabian Sea.\nReason: The Portuguese fleet was forced to retreat to their southern base in Cochin.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The victory allowed the coalition to consolidate their forces at Diu.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements regarding the Battle of Chaul:\n1. It was fought in 1508 CE.\n2. The Portuguese fleet was commanded by Francisco de Almeida personally.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; the fleet was commanded by Lourenço de Almeida.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements about the Mamluk fleet at Chaul:\n1. It was led by Amir Husain Al-Kurdi.\n2. The ships were constructed at Suez using timber supplied by Venice.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Both statements are correct. Amir Husain led the Mamluk fleet built at Suez with Venetian timber.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to Malik Ayyaz, consider these statements:\n1. He was the governor of Cochin.\n2. He co-commanded the coalition forces at Chaul.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 1, 'sol': 'Statement 2 is correct. Statement 1 is incorrect; he was the governor of Diu.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': "Consider the statements about Lourenço de Almeida's flagship at Chaul:\n1. It was trapped in the estuary due to a sea cable.\n2. It successfully broke the blockade and returned to Lisbon.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?", 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. The flagship was sunk and Lourenço died; it did not return.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the aftermath of the battle, consider these statements:\n1. The Portuguese prisoners were executed by Malik Ayyaz.\n2. Viceroy Almeida accepted his replacement by Albuquerque immediately.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both statements are incorrect. Prisoners were treated well, and Almeida refused to step down.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did the Mamluk Sultanate decide to intervene militarily in the Indian Ocean in 1507?', 'sol': 'The Portuguese blockade of the Red Sea cut off Mamluk customs revenues from the spice trade, threatening the economic survival of Egypt.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why was the harbor of Chaul tactically disadvantageous for the Portuguese fleet?', 'sol': 'The shallow estuary and narrow channels restricted the mobility of the large Portuguese naus, making them vulnerable to light, fast Gujarati dhows.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did Venice secretly support the Mamluks against the Portuguese?', 'sol': 'Venetian trade depended on buying spices in Egypt; the Portuguese direct Cape Route bypassed Venice, destroying its commercial dominance in Europe.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did Malik Ayyaz use his position as governor of Diu to support the Mamluk fleet?', 'sol': 'He provided Diu as a naval base, supplied fresh provisions, and reinforced the Mamluk fleet with his own coastal gunboats.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the death of Lourenço de Almeida impact the Portuguese chain of command in India?', 'sol': 'It caused a crisis, as Francisco de Almeida refused to hand over power to his designated successor Albuquerque, prioritizing personal revenge.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the coalition fleet manage to trap the Portuguese flagship at Chaul?', 'sol': 'They damaged its rudder with cannon fire, and a Gujarati cable caught the ship, pinning it down in the river channel.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Analyze the geopolitical motivations of the Mamluk-Ottoman-Gujarati coalition at Chaul.', 'sol': 'The coalition aimed to protect their joint trade interests from Portuguese monopoly, combining Egyptian naval ambition, Ottoman gunnery, and Gujarati local power.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': "Examine the role of chivalric codes and military honor in Lourenço de Almeida's tactical decisions at Chaul.", 'sol': 'His refusal to abandon the trapped flagship, despite being wounded and urged by his captains to escape, led to his death but created a legendary martyr for the Portuguese empire.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Discuss the diplomatic strategy of Malik Ayyaz in the treatment of Portuguese prisoners.', 'sol': 'Ayyaz treated prisoners well to preserve a line of negotiation with Lisbon, recognizing that a brutal execution would invite total destruction from the Viceroy.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain the tactical differences between Mamluk dhows and Portuguese naus.', 'sol': 'Mamluk dhows were fast and agile but lightly built, while Portuguese naus were large, heavily armed with cannons, but less maneuverable in shallow waters.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Describe the chain of events that led to the Battle of Chaul.', 'sol': 'Portuguese patrols blockaded the Red Sea; Egypt built a fleet at Suez with Venetian help, sailed to India, allied with the Governor of Diu, and intercepted the Portuguese patrol at Chaul.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain why the Battle of Chaul is considered a turning point in early Indo-Portuguese history.', 'sol': 'It was the first time a local coalition successfully defeated the Portuguese navy, showing that European naval power could be challenged with coordinated tactics.'}]

section4_hi = [{'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'पुर्तगालियों और एक संयुक्त मुस्लिम बेड़े के बीच चोल (Chaul) की लड़ाई किस वर्ष हुई थी?', 'opts': ['1508 ईस्वी', '1505 ईस्वी', '1509 ईस्वी', '1515 ईस्वी'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'चोल (Chaul) की लड़ाई मार्च 1508 ईस्वी में लड़ी गई थी।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'चोल की लड़ाई में मारा गया युवा पुर्तगाली कमांडर कौन था?', 'opts': ['लॉरेंको डी अल्मेडा', 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा', 'अल्फांसो डी अल्बुकर्क', 'डुआर्टे पाचेको परेरा'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'वायसराय के एकमात्र पुत्र लॉरेंको डी अल्मेडा की मृत्यु तब हुई जब उनका प्रमुख जहाज घिर गया और डूब गया।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'किस मिस्र के राजवंश ने चोल में पुर्तगालियों से लड़ने के लिए अमीर हुसैन अल-कुर्दी के नेतृत्व में बेड़ा भेजा था?', 'opts': ['ममलुक सल्तनत', 'ओटोमन साम्राज्य', 'फातिमी खिलाफत', 'अय्यूबीड राजवंश'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'मिस्र के ममलुक सल्तनत ने अपने मसाला व्यापार हितों की रक्षा के लिए बेड़ा भेजा था।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'दीव का गवर्नर कौन था जिसने गुजराती बेड़े की कमान संभाली और चोल में ममलुकों के साथ गठबंधन किया?', 'opts': ['मलिक अय्याज़', 'बहादुर शाह', 'मुजफ्फर शाह द्वितीय', 'महमूद बेगड़ा'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'मलिक अय्याज़ (दीव के गवर्नर) ने गठबंधन बेड़े की सह-कमान संभाली थी।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'पुर्तगाली बेड़े के लिए चोल की लड़ाई का अंत कैसे हुआ?', 'opts': ['इसके परिणामस्वरूप एक निर्णायक हार हुई और उनका प्रमुख जहाज नष्ट हो गया', 'यह पुर्तगालियों की एक निर्णायक जीत थी', 'यह एक शांतिपूर्ण ड्रॉ था', 'पुर्तगाली बेड़े को पूरी तरह से पकड़ लिया गया था'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'यह लड़ाई पुर्तगालियों के लिए एक बड़ी हार थी, जिसके परिणामस्वरूप लॉरेंको की मृत्यु हुई और उनका जहाज डूब गया।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'चोल में पुर्तगालियों को हराने वाले संबद्ध गठबंधन में कौन से बेड़े शामिल थे? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['अमीर हुसैन के तहत ममलुक बेड़ा', 'मलिक अय्याज़ के तहत गुजरात सल्तनत का बेड़ा', 'कालीकट के ज़मोरिन की सेनाएँ', 'ब्रिटिश रॉयल नेवी'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'गठबंधन में ममलुक, गुजराती और कालीकट के जहाज शामिल थे। ब्रिटिश इसमें शामिल नहीं थे।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'चोल में लॉरेंको डी अल्मेडा की मृत्यु के प्रमुख विवरणों की पहचान करें। (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['उनका प्रमुख जहाज नदी में एक गुजराती केबल द्वारा फंस गया था', 'घायल होने के बावजूद उन्होंने पीछे हटने या आत्मसमर्पण करने से इनकार कर दिया', 'वह एक तोप के गोले की चपेट में आने से मारे गए थे', 'उन्हें पकड़ लिया गया था और काहिरा में फांसी दे दी गई थी'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'उनका जहाज फंस गया था, उन्होंने आत्मसमर्पण से इनकार किया, और तोप के गोले से उनकी मौत हुई। उन्हें काहिरा नहीं ले जाया गया था।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'चोल में पुर्तगाली हार में किन कारकों ने योगदान दिया? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['भारतीय जल क्षेत्र में ममलुक बेड़े का अचानक आगमन', 'उथले नदी बंदरगाह में पुर्तगाली जहाजों का रणनीतिक रूप से फंसना', 'तटीय गनबोटों के साथ मलिक अय्याज़ का समन्वित हमला', 'लड़ाई के दौरान पुर्तगाली कप्तानों का विद्रोह'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'ममलुकों का अचानक आगमन, उथली नदी में फंसना और मलिक अय्याज़ के गनबोट प्रमुख कारक थे। वहां कोई विद्रोह नहीं हुआ था।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'चोल की लड़ाई की तत्काल राजनीतिक प्रतिक्रियाएँ क्या थीं? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा ने व्यक्तिगत बदला लेने की शपथ ली', 'हिंद महासागर में पुर्तगाली प्रतिष्ठा को अस्थायी रूप से झटका लगा', 'अल्मेडा ने अल्बुकर्क को सत्ता सौंपने से इनकार कर दिया', 'ज़मोरिन ने कोचीन पर तुरंत कब्जा कर लिया'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'अल्मेडा ने बदला लेने की कसम खाई, पुर्तगाली प्रतिष्ठा को झटका लगा, और सत्ता का हस्तांतरण टाल दिया गया।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'चोल की लड़ाई में मलिक अय्याज़ की भूमिका का वर्णन करने वाले विवरणों का चयन करें: (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['उन्होंने दीव के गवर्नर के रूप में कार्य किया', 'उन्होंने गुजरात के तेज तटीय जहाजों और गनबोटों की कमान संभाली', 'राजनयिक लाभ बनाए रखने के लिए पुर्तगाली बेड़े को पूरी तरह से नष्ट करने से बचते हुए, उन्होंने समझदारी से काम लिया', 'वह एक पुर्तगाली एजेंट थे जिन्होंने ज़मोरिन को धोखा दिया था'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'अय्याज़ दीव के गवर्नर थे, उन्होंने गुजरात बेड़े का नेतृत्व किया, और रणनीतिक कारणों से समझदारी से काम लिया।'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The Battle of Chaul was the first major defeat suffered by the Portuguese in Indian waters.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'It shattered their myth of naval invincibility.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Amir Husain Al-Kurdi was the commander of the Mamluk fleet dispatched from Egypt.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'He led the Mamluk expedition to expel the Portuguese.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'लॉरेंको डी अल्मेडा surrendered his ship to मलिक अय्याज़ before dying.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He refused to surrender and fought until he was killed by a cannonball.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The Battle of Chaul was fought in the open ocean far away from the coast.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'It was fought inside the shallow harbor and estuary of Chaul.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The Portuguese fleet at Chaul was caught by surprise because they did not expect Mamluk intervention.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'They did not know that a Mamluk fleet had arrived in India.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Francisco de अल्मेडा was present and personally commanded the fleet at Chaul.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'The fleet was commanded by his son Lourenço; Francisco was in Cochin.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'मलिक अय्याज़ treated the Portuguese prisoners captured at Chaul with cruelty.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He treated them with relative kindness to preserve diplomatic options with Lisbon.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The battle ended the Mamluk spice monopoly permanently.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'It was a victory for the Mamluks, temporarily securing their trade route.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Battle of Chaul was fought in the month of __________ in 1508.', 'ans': 'March', 'sol': 'The naval clash occurred in March 1508 CE.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Egyptian commander of the fleet at Chaul was Amir __________.', 'ans': 'Husain', 'sol': 'Amir Husain Al-Kurdi led the Mamluk forces.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The governor of Diu who co-commanded the coalition forces was Malik __________.', 'ans': 'Ayyaz', 'sol': 'Malik Ayyaz was the governor of Diu under the Gujarat Sultanate.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': "The Viceroy's son, __________ de अल्मेडा, died in the battle.", 'ans': 'Lourenço', 'sol': 'Lourenço de अल्मेडा was the commander at Chaul.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The flagship at Chaul was trapped when its hull was pierced and it was caught by a sea __________.', 'ans': 'cable', 'sol': 'A cable caught the ship, preventing it from escaping the harbor.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Muslim coalition was backed by the Sultan of Gujarat, Mahmud __________.', 'ans': 'Begarha', 'sol': 'Mahmud Begarha was the famous sultan of Gujarat.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The battle took place in the harbor of __________, a port near modern Mumbai.', 'ans': 'Chaul', 'sol': 'Chaul was a major trade port on the western coast.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Mamluk fleet had been built in the Red Sea using timber supplied by __________.', 'ans': 'Venice', 'sol': 'Venice secretly supplied ship-building timber to help Egypt fight Portugal.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'चोल के युद्ध कमांडरों का उनके संबद्ध संगठनों से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'लॉरेंको डी अल्मेडा'}, {'left': 'अमीर हुसैन अल-कुर्दी'}, {'left': 'मलिक अय्याज़'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'पुर्तगाली क्राउन बेड़ा'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'मिस्र का ममलुक सल्तनत'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'गुजरात सल्तनत (दीव)'}], 'sol': 'लॉरेंको पुर्तगाली थे, अमीर हुसैन ममलुक थे, और अय्याज़ गुजरात से थे।'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'लड़ाई के रणनीतिक परिणामों का संबंधित संस्थाओं से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'लॉरेंको की मृत्यु'}, {'left': 'कैदियों के साथ दयालु व्यवहार'}, {'left': 'जहाज निर्माण लकड़ी की आपूर्ति'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा का दुख और सत्ता हस्तांतरण में देरी'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'मलिक अय्याज़ की सतर्क कूटनीति'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'ममलुकों को वेनिस का गुप्त समर्थन'}], 'sol': 'लॉरेंको की मृत्यु से अल्मेडा को गहरा दुख हुआ, अय्याज़ ने कैदियों से अच्छा व्यवहार किया, और वेनिस ने लकड़ी की आपूर्ति की।'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'लड़ाई की भौगोलिक विशेषताओं का उनके महत्व से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'चोल मुहाना'}, {'left': 'स्वेज शिपयार्ड'}, {'left': 'दीव बंदरगाह'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'पुर्तगाली जहाजों के लिए उथला पानी का जाल'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'ममलुक बेड़े का निर्माण स्थल'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'गुजरात गठबंधन बेड़े का आधार'}], 'sol': 'चोल मुहाना उथला जाल था, स्वेज ममलुक बेड़े का निर्माण स्थल था, और दीव मलिक अय्याज़ का आधार था।'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What weapon killed लॉरेंको डी अल्मेडा?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: A cannonball.। स्पष्टीकरण: He was struck by a cannonball after his legs were shattered by a previous shot.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which European power secretly assisted the Mamluks in building their fleet?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Venice.। स्पष्टीकरण: Venice wanted to protect its Levantine trade monopoly.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What did मलिक अय्याज़ do with the surviving Portuguese prisoners?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: He imprisoned them in Diu and treated them well.। स्पष्टीकरण: He kept them as diplomatic hostages.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "How did Lourenço's ship become trapped at Chaul?", 'sol': 'उत्तर: Its rudder was damaged and it was caught by a fish trap/cable.। स्पष्टीकरण: The ship could not maneuver in the shallow estuary.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "Did the Portuguese fleet retreat after Lourenço's death?", 'sol': 'उत्तर: Yes, the remaining ships withdrew to Cochin.। स्पष्टीकरण: The survivors sailed south under the second-in-command.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Who was the sultan of Egypt who ordered the creation of the anti-Portuguese fleet?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Al-Ashraf Qansuh al-Ghawri.। स्पष्टीकरण: He was the penultimate Mamluk Sultan.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What was the reaction of the Zamorin of Calicut to the Battle of Chaul?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: He celebrated and sent reinforcements to the Mamluks.। स्पष्टीकरण: He hoped to finally expel the Portuguese from Malabar.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Why did the Portuguese not expect the Mamluk fleet at Chaul?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: They believed the Mamluks lacked the naval capacity to sail into the Indian Ocean.। स्पष्टीकरण: The Mamluks had traditionally relied on land armies and lacked a navy.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: The Mamluk fleet was able to surprise the Portuguese at Chaul.\nकारण: The Portuguese did not have an active intelligence network in the Red Sea in 1507.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Lack of intelligence allowed the Mamluk fleet to sail to India undetected.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Lourenço de अल्मेडा refused to abandon his flagship.\nकारण: He believed that a Portuguese noble commander should never surrender to Muslim forces.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Chivalric codes of honor prevented him from retreating.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Venice secretly supplied timber to the Mamluks to build their war fleet.\nकारण: Venice wanted to destroy the Mamluk Sultanate and take over Egypt.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Assertion is true, but Reason is false because Venice wanted to help Egypt preserve the spice route from Portuguese disruption.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Malik Ayyaz was a native Gujarati noble.\nकारण: He was born in Ahmedabad and belonged to the royal family of the Gujarat Sultanate.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. Malik Ayyaz was a Russian slave convert who rose to become the governor of Diu.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "अभिकथन: The Battle of Chaul resulted in the complete destruction of the Portuguese navy in India.\nकारण: All 21 ships of अल्मेडा's fleet were sunk during the battle.", 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. Only a few Portuguese ships were lost, including the flagship; the rest withdrew safely.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Francisco de अल्मेडा was devastated by the news of the Battle of Chaul.\nकारण: His only son Lourenço was killed, and the Portuguese navy had suffered its first defeat.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The loss of his son transformed his governorship into a campaign of revenge.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Malik Ayyaz treated the Portuguese prisoners kindly.\nकारण: He wanted to keep a diplomatic door open with the Viceroy in case the Portuguese retaliated.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Ayyaz acted pragmatically, anticipating a strong Portuguese counter-attack.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: The Battle of Chaul temporarily secured Mamluk-Gujarati control over the Arabian Sea.\nकारण: The Portuguese fleet was forced to retreat to their southern base in Cochin.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The victory allowed the coalition to consolidate their forces at Diu.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements regarding the Battle of Chaul:\n1. It was fought in 1508 CE.\n2. The Portuguese fleet was commanded by Francisco de अल्मेडा personally.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; the fleet was commanded by Lourenço de अल्मेडा.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements about the Mamluk fleet at Chaul:\n1. It was led by Amir Husain Al-Kurdi.\n2. The ships were constructed at Suez using timber supplied by Venice.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Both statements are correct. Amir Husain led the Mamluk fleet built at Suez with Venetian timber.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to मलिक अय्याज़, consider these statements:\n1. He was the governor of Cochin.\n2. He co-commanded the coalition forces at Chaul.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 1, 'sol': 'Statement 2 is correct. Statement 1 is incorrect; he was the governor of Diu.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': "Consider the statements about Lourenço de अल्मेडा's flagship at Chaul:\n1. It was trapped in the estuary due to a sea cable.\n2. It successfully broke the blockade and returned to Lisbon.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?", 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. The flagship was sunk and Lourenço died; it did not return.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the aftermath of the battle, consider these statements:\n1. The Portuguese prisoners were executed by मलिक अय्याज़.\n2. Viceroy अल्मेडा accepted his replacement by Albuquerque immediately.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both statements are incorrect. Prisoners were treated well, and अल्मेडा refused to step down.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did the Mamluk Sultanate decide to intervene militarily in the Indian Ocean in 1507?', 'sol': 'The Portuguese blockade of the Red Sea cut off Mamluk customs revenues from the spice trade, threatening the economic survival of Egypt.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why was the harbor of Chaul tactically disadvantageous for the Portuguese fleet?', 'sol': 'The shallow estuary and narrow channels restricted the mobility of the large Portuguese naus, making them vulnerable to light, fast Gujarati dhows.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did Venice secretly support the Mamluks against the Portuguese?', 'sol': 'Venetian trade depended on buying spices in Egypt; the Portuguese direct Cape Route bypassed Venice, destroying its commercial dominance in Europe.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did मलिक अय्याज़ use his position as governor of Diu to support the Mamluk fleet?', 'sol': 'He provided Diu as a naval base, supplied fresh provisions, and reinforced the Mamluk fleet with his own coastal gunboats.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the death of Lourenço de अल्मेडा impact the Portuguese chain of command in India?', 'sol': 'It caused a crisis, as Francisco de अल्मेडा refused to hand over power to his designated successor Albuquerque, prioritizing personal revenge.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the coalition fleet manage to trap the Portuguese flagship at Chaul?', 'sol': 'They damaged its rudder with cannon fire, and a Gujarati cable caught the ship, pinning it down in the river channel.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Analyze the geopolitical motivations of the Mamluk-Ottoman-Gujarati coalition at Chaul.', 'sol': 'The coalition aimed to protect their joint trade interests from Portuguese monopoly, combining Egyptian naval ambition, Ottoman gunnery, and Gujarati local power.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': "Examine the role of chivalric codes and military honor in Lourenço de अल्मेडा's tactical decisions at Chaul.", 'sol': 'His refusal to abandon the trapped flagship, despite being wounded and urged by his captains to escape, led to his death but created a legendary martyr for the Portuguese empire.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Discuss the diplomatic strategy of मलिक अय्याज़ in the treatment of Portuguese prisoners.', 'sol': 'Ayyaz treated prisoners well to preserve a line of negotiation with Lisbon, recognizing that a brutal execution would invite total destruction from the Viceroy.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain the tactical differences between Mamluk dhows and Portuguese naus.', 'sol': 'Mamluk dhows were fast and agile but lightly built, while Portuguese naus were large, heavily armed with cannons, but less maneuverable in shallow waters.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Describe the chain of events that led to the Battle of Chaul.', 'sol': 'Portuguese patrols blockaded the Red Sea; Egypt built a fleet at Suez with Venetian help, sailed to India, allied with the Governor of Diu, and intercepted the Portuguese patrol at Chaul.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain why the Battle of Chaul is considered a turning point in early Indo-Portuguese history.', 'sol': 'It was the first time a local coalition successfully defeated the Portuguese navy, showing that European naval power could be challenged with coordinated tactics.'}]
